{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuimDMivtUHsCzKePwZj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Not reliably. The Agents SDK expects every Agent instance to have a **name**. It uses that name for state, routing, and helpers like `this.name`. A stub you build yourself with `env.MY_AGENT.newUniqueId()` and `env.MY_AGENT.get(id)` never gets a name set, so RPC calls on it are likely to fail, often with an error about reading `.name` before it was set.\n\nThe supported way is `getAgentByName(env.MY_AGENT, someName)`, which sets the name before you call methods. If you need a unique ID, generate one yourself (for example `crypto.randomUUID()`) and pass it as the name.\n\nI answered this from memory, not the current docs, so check the Agents SDK documentation if you're on a recent version."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5829,"cache_read_input_tokens":15764,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5829},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b10e8de-4990-4a73-91ef-e032540c9424","uuid":"cd420cb7-bfb8-411a-94c4-9c44f575aafc","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:14:05.454Z","request_id":"req_011CfuimD7aosuhXjCpihXTD"}
